server-info-introduction-button = Tutorial

intro-skip-button = Skip introduction
intro-gotcha-button = Got it
intro-lobby-ready-up-button-desc = Press the join button when you are ready to start playing!
intro-click-to-continue-label = Click here to continue...
intro-click-any-to-continue-label = Click anywhere to continue...

intro-info-complete = Introduction complete! You can now begin your adventure on the space station. Good luck!
intro-begin-error-already-running = The introduction is already running.
intro-begin-error-outside-lobby = You cannot start the introduction outside the lobby screen.
intro-progress-update-error-invalid-session = Cannot update introduction progress without a valid player session.
intro-progress-update-error-invalid-contentdata = Cannot update introduction progress without valid session content data.

cmd-startintro-help = Starts the introduction for new players.
cmd-startintro-not-in-lobby = You must be in the lobby to start the introduction.

cmd-cancelintro-help = Cancels the ongoing introduction.

intro-welcome-message-1 = [bold]Get ready![/bold] You have just been assigned aboard a [color=purple][bold]Space Station[/bold][/color], and from this moment on you are part of an adventure like nothing you have experienced before!
intro-welcome-message-2 = Yes, our game is hard and complex - [bold]that is the charm![/bold] But you do not have to learn everything alone...
intro-welcome-message-3 = [bold]We are here to teach you everything![/bold] Give yourself a chance to enjoy this immersive fun ;)
intro-welcome-begin-agree-button = Yes, walk me through the tutorial!
intro-welcome-begin-disagree-button = No, I want to start playing right away!
intro-welcome-reminder-message = Remember, you can always start the introduction tutorial later by pressing the [bold]{$server-info-introduction-button}[/bold] button on the lobby screen!

intro-lobby-overview-message-1 = This section shows information about the [bold]current round[/bold] and [bold]your character[/bold], and below it is the [bold]chat window[/bold].
intro-lobby-overview-character-section-message-1 = Let's look at the character section. Do not worry about those icons - they are just [bold]preferred job settings[/bold] you can choose before the round starts. We will explain everything in a moment!
intro-lobby-overview-character-section-message-2 = Click [bold]"{$intro-lobby-overview-character-editor-button}"[/bold] to open your character editor.

intro-character-creation-message-1 = In the character editor you can [bold]customize the look of your characters[/bold], [bold]set job preferences[/bold], and other options.
intro-character-creation-message-2 = Try setting [bold]your character's appearance[/bold] in this tab! You can freely change [bold]gender, species, skin, hair and eye color[/bold], as well as [bold]clothing and accessories[/bold].
intro-character-creation-message-3 = Great! Now go to the [bold]"{$humanoid-profile-editor-jobs-tab}"[/bold] tab to set your job preferences. Here you can pick the roles you would like to play. Each job has duties you can learn about in the [bold]Guidebook[/bold]. If you are new to SS14, we recommend roles like [bold]Janitor, Service Worker, or Botanist[/bold], as they are more newcomer-friendly.
intro-character-creation-click-job-priorities-button = Click [bold]"{$character-setup-gui-edit-job-priorities-button}"[/bold] to set job priorities.
intro-character-creation-message-4 = Here you can set [bold]job priorities[/bold] that decide how much you want to play a given role. You can set priorities to [bold]High, Medium, Low, or Never[/bold]. Higher priority jobs are more likely to be assigned. Try setting priorities for a few roles you like, [bold]and do not forget to save your changes![/bold]
intro-character-creation-click-back-to-setup-button = When you are done, click your character banner to return to the editor.
intro-character-creation-message-5 = In this tab you can also choose whether you want to play as an [bold]antagonist[/bold] (traitor, saboteur, etc.) and set a priority for those roles. If you are new to SS14, we recommend learning the game with regular jobs first.
intro-character-creation-message-6 = Now go to the [bold]"{$humanoid-profile-editor-traits-tab}"[/bold] tab. Here you can pick [bold]extra traits[/bold] that give your character unique skills or limitations. Remember each trait has a [bold]point cost[/bold], so choose wisely! Try picking a few traits if you want.
intro-character-creation-message-7 = Nice! Almost done - go to the [bold]"{$humanoid-profile-editor-markings-tab}"[/bold] tab to add [bold]markings[/bold] like tattoos, scars, or makeup. A great way to give your character personality!
intro-character-creation-message-8 = [italic]Perfect![/italic] Now go to [bold]"{$humanoid-profile-editor-cd-records-tab}"[/bold] to fill in your character's [bold]medical and personal information[/bold].
intro-character-creation-final-message = Your character looks fantastic and is ready to go! You can always return to the character editor to make changes before the round starts.
intro-character-creation-save-reminder-message = Do not forget to click [bold]"{$humanoid-profile-editor-save-button}"[/bold] to save all changes.
intro-character-creation-click-to-continue-button = When you are done, click here to continue

intro-proceed-prompt-message-1 = Great! You have already learned almost everything!
intro-welcome-begin-question-message = [bold]Do you want to continue to the practical part of the tutorial, where you can try your skills on a simulated space station?[/bold]
intro-proceed-prompt-agree-button = Yes!
intro-proceed-prompt-disagree-button = Maybe later
intro-proceed-prompt-agree-later = No problem! Remember you can always start the practical tutorial later by clicking the marked button. Good luck!
intro-solitary-server-hopping-message = Hang tight, transferring you to the simulated space station...
intro-proceed-prompt-fallback-message = You already know almost everything! Feel free to join the game - the crew will gladly welcome you and help with your first steps. When you have a moment, check the guidebook to learn more about mechanics and your role. Good luck and have fun!
